prompt:
Paint ONE complete fantasy WORLD MAP of a single continent as an OLD PARCHMENT CHART, in the style of a hand-drawn, hand-inked and watercoloured antique cartographer's map (a treasured explorer's atlas page): aged cream and tan parchment with soft stains, foxing, faint fold creases and darker burnt edges; brown-black ink linework with fine hatching; muted watercolour washes (sea teal-blue, forest greens, ochre desert, grey-white snowfields, olive marsh, charcoal and rust volcanic wastes). Seen from directly above, as a map, NOT a landscape painting and NOT pixel art.

The attached image is a rough LAYOUT GUIDE of the continent drawn as flat colour blocks (dark blue = sea). Keep the same overall arrangement and relative positions and sizes of the lands and seas (the map will be matched to the game's places), but redraw every coastline, border and shape as NATURAL, organic, irregular cartography: no straight edges, no rectangles, no grid. The regions, following the guide:
- the NORTH-WEST: a snowy highland with small ink-drawn snowy mountain peaks, fir trees and a round frozen lake at its west;
- the WEST: a vast ancient FOREST of many little inked tree crowns, with one COLOSSAL tree drawn larger than everything else in its south-west, and a narrow river;
- between them and to the east of the forest: open NORTH PLAINS of grass;
- in the CENTRE: a green PENINSULA / island surrounded by an inland sea, joined to the north plains by a small drawbridge at its north tip; a tiny LIGHTHOUSE on its southern cape and a tiny harbour town on its east coast, a small village on a hill in its west;
- in the SOUTH-WEST: a golden DESERT with dunes drawn as little ink curves, a small oasis and a half-buried giant statue;
- along the SOUTH: dark VOLCANIC ASH WASTES with a big smoking VOLCANO (a tiny red glow at its top) and lava streams;
- in the EAST across the inland sea: a misty MARSH of reeds with a lake town and a little bell tower;
- a mountain range crossing the north between the snow and the plains, and a mountain road to the north-east;
- farther lands at the edges (north-east highlands, the south-east island coast, small scattered islands in the outer sea) drawn more faintly, as unexplored coasts.
Also draw: tiny pictorial ink landmarks (towns as clusters of tiny roofs, a castle-less world of villages), dotted travel roads connecting the regions, rows of little mountains with shaded sides, forests as clusters of tiny tree crowns, rhumb lines and small ink waves in the seas, a sea serpent and a small sailing ship in the outer sea, an ornate COMPASS ROSE in the lower right sea, and a decorative inked BORDER frame with corner ornaments around the whole map.
ABSOLUTELY NO TEXT: no letters, no words, no labels, no numbers, no cartouche with writing, no signature (place names are added later by the game). No UI, no characters.
